    StoryModel(
      id: 'featured_destiny_compassion_community',
      authorUid: 'trusted-featured',
      authorName: 'Destiny A.',
      title: 'You Do Not Have to Carry It Alone',
      content: 'Destiny learned that loneliness was not always about being physically alone.\n\nA person could sit in a crowded room and still feel unreachable.\n\nShe could answer messages, attend ordinary events, smile at people, and still carry a private weight that nobody knew how to name.\n\nFor a while, she thought hiding that weight was a form of strength.\n\nIf nobody knew, nobody could misunderstand.\n\nIf nobody knew, nobody could judge.\n\nIf nobody knew, she would not have to explain.\n\nBut hiding pain has a cost.\n\nIt makes every difficult thought echo louder.\n\nOne day, Destiny noticed that she was spending more energy pretending she was okay than actually taking care of herself.\n\nThat realization scared her.\n\nWhat would happen if she told someone the truth?\n\nShe chose one person.\n\nNot everyone.\n\nNot a room full of people.\n\nOne person she trusted.\n\nThe conversation was awkward.\n\nThere were pauses.\n\nThere were sentences she could not finish.\n\nBut the other person did not demand a perfect explanation.\n\nThey listened.\n\nThat was the beginning.\n\nNot a cure.\n\nNot a miracle.\n\nA beginning.\n\nDestiny discovered that being understood did not require another person to experience exactly what she experienced.\n\nSometimes understanding simply meant someone was willing to stay.',
